#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/simd/index.rst:122
msgid "Module Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/simd/index.rst:128
msgid ""
"``a, b = ...`` emits two ``pair_get`` calls against the pair. The pair- "
"producing op (e.g. ``vintlv``, ``vld2``, or post-update ``vld``) is bound "
"once at its call site by the frontend, so both ``pair_get`` calls reference "
"a single bound variable rather than inlining the pair expression twice."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/simd/index.rst:133
msgid ""
"``dtype`` is a pair describing both result types, such as the ``(boolx256, "
"int32x64)`` carry/result pair returned by ``vaddc``. Omitting it defaults "
"both result types to the dtype of the backing TIR expression."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/simd/index.rst:151
msgid ""
"Returns a vector_bool (boolx256). dist: \"PAT_ALL\", \"PAT_VL1\".."
"\"PAT_VL128\", \"PAT_M3\", \"PAT_M4\", \"PAT_H\", \"PAT_Q\", etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/simd/index.rst:0
msgid "Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/simd/index.rst:199
msgid ""
"Uses ``local.var`` scope and behaves as one vector register value. For an "
"addressable array of registers (``v[i]``), use :func:`alloc_local`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/simd/index.rst:207
msgid ""
"Uses ``local`` scope so each element is an individually addressable "
"register, allowing indexed access like ``v[i]``::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/simd/index.rst:210
msgid ""
"v = T.simd.alloc_local(4, \"float32\")\n"
"for i in T.Unroll(4, explicit=True):\n"
"    v[i] = vld(s_ub[i * VL])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/simd/index.rst:229
msgid ""
"addr can be a BufferLoad auto-wrapped as tl.access_ptr. Express address "
"offsets in ``addr``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/simd/index.rst:232
msgid ""
"With ``post_inc=step``, load through a mutable :func:`make_ubuf_ptr` handle "
"and return ``(vector, advanced_pointer)``. Assign the second result back to "
"the handle. ``step`` is a signed int32 increment in elements of the dtype "
"declared by :func:`make_ubuf_ptr`; the load uses the old address. The dtype "
"must be 8/16/32-bit and match the distribution. ``None`` selects an ordinary "
"load; zero still returns the pair without advancing the pointer::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/simd/index.rst:239
msgid ""
"src_ptr = T.simd.make_ubuf_ptr(T.access_ptr(src_ub[0], \"r\", extent=256), "
"\"uint16\")\n"
"first, src_ptr = T.simd.vld(src_ptr, post_inc=128)\n"
"second, src_ptr = T.simd.vld(src_ptr, post_inc=128)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/simd/index.rst:243
msgid ""
"Keep the pointer within one SIMD VF and declare its complete accessed span "
"in the initializer's ``access_ptr``, as in the example."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/simd/index.rst:246
msgid ""
"A ``BRC_B8/B16/B32`` broadcast replicates one element of the width named by "
"the suffix, widening the result past the source buffer's element type when "
"the two differ (``BRC_B16`` over a ``uint8`` buffer broadcasts a 16-bit "
"element, not a byte). Every other distribution takes its element width from "
"the source buffer; their ``_B*`` suffixes describe the data being loaded and "
"must agree with it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/simd/index.rst:258
msgid "Supported dists:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/simd/index.rst:259
msgid "``DINTLV_B8``: load 512xu8/fp8 -> two 256-lane regs (even/odd bytes)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/simd/index.rst:260
msgid "``DINTLV_B16``: load 256xbf16/u16 -> two 128-lane regs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/simd/index.rst:261
msgid "``DINTLV_B32``: load 128xf32/u32 -> two 64-lane regs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/simd/index.rst:263
msgid ""
"The access_ptr footprint is always 2x the single-vector width. This is an "
"opaque memory load: the pair is bound once at this program point so the two "
"``pair_get`` calls from the unpack share a single load rather than issuing "
"two independent loads."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/simd/index.rst:273
msgid ""
"addr can be a BufferLoad auto-wrapped as tl.access_ptr. Express address "
"offsets in ``addr``. Optional ``extent`` overrides the default access_ptr "
"footprint (e.g. 8 for a dense PAT_VL8 NORM_B16 recip pack)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/simd/index.rst:283
msgid ""
"Passing a regular buffer access performs a store and returns ``void``. Set "
"``update=True`` with the mutable handle returned by :func:`make_ubuf_ptr` to "
"enable POST_UPDATE and return the advanced pointer, which should be assigned "
"back to the same handle::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/simd/index.rst:288
#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/simd/index.rst:304
msgid ""
"dst_ptr = T.simd.make_ubuf_ptr(dst_ub[0], \"bfloat16\")\n"
"dst_ptr = T.simd.vsstb(src, dst_ptr, stride, mask, update=True)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/simd/index.rst:296
msgid ""
"``dtype`` declares the pointee element type used by :func:`vld` and checked "
"against the source vector by :func:`vsstb`. It is stored in the enclosing "
"block's IR annotations; the mutable carrier remains a ``handle`` buffer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/simd/index.rst:300
msgid ""
"The pointer is carried by a ``local.var`` handle buffer. Assigning the "
"advanced handle returned by :func:`vld` or :func:`vsstb` writes it back into "
"the same mutable carrier::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/simd/index.rst:314
msgid ""
"``carry`` is a ``boolx256`` predicate register and ``result`` has the same "
"dtype as the inputs. The underlying Ascend ``vaddc`` instruction only "
"supports full-register ``int32x64`` and ``uint32x64`` operands."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/simd/index.rst:323
msgid "``carry`` is 1 where the subtraction completes without borrow."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/simd/index.rst:364
msgid ""
"``bin=0`` counts values in ``[0, 127]`` and ``bin=1`` counts values in "
"``[128, 255]``. The destination register is updated in place."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/simd/index.rst:372
msgid ""
"``bin=0`` returns cumulative counts through values ``[0, 127]`` and "
"``bin=1`` returns cumulative counts through values ``[128, 255]``. The "
"destination register is updated in place."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/simd/index.rst:381
msgid ""
"``precision=None`` follows ``tl.enable_fast_math`` (precise fp32 division "
"when fast math is off, hardware instruction otherwise). Non-fp32 division "
"always uses the hardware instruction."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/simd/index.rst:385
msgid "``precision`` selects the implementation per op:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/simd/index.rst:387
msgid "``'ftz_true'``: bare hardware SFU (flush-to-zero semantics)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/simd/index.rst:388
msgid ""
"``'exact'`` (alias ``'vdiv_0ulp_ftz_true'``): correctly-rounded fp32 "
"division (CANN DivAlgo::PRECISION_0ULP_FTZ_TRUE / DivPrecisionImpl)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/simd/index.rst:391
msgid "Requires float32 for precise paths."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/simd/index.rst:436
msgid "dtype_str specifies the target vector element type (e.g. \"float32\")."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/simd/index.rst:443
msgid "pos: \"POS_LOWEST\" (lane 0) or \"POS_HIGHEST\" (lane N)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/simd/index.rst:450
msgid ""
"The sums of adjacent source lanes are packed into the low half of the result "
"vector. Supported types: float32, float16."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/simd/index.rst:498
msgid ""
"dst[lane] = index + lane (INC_ORDER) / index - lane (DEC_ORDER). dtype_str "
"is the destination vector element type (e.g. \"int32\", \"float32\")."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/simd/index.rst:506
#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/simd/index.rst:513
msgid "op: eq/ne/gt/ge/lt/le."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/simd/index.rst:520
msgid "Unpack: a, b = vintlv(x, y)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/simd/index.rst:522
#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/simd/index.rst:533
msgid ""
"The pair is bound once at the call site so the unpack's two ``pair_get`` "
"calls share a single permutation instruction instead of inlining the pair "
"expression twice."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/simd/index.rst:531
msgid "Unpack: a, b = vdintlv(x, y)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/simd/index.rst:547
msgid "Supports u32->u16 and u16->u8 (needed for dense UE8M0 scale packing)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/simd/index.rst:569
msgid ""
"Write-side counterpart to vgatherb/vgather2. ``index`` is a vector register "
"of per-lane element offsets (uint32 for 32-bit elements, uint16 for 8/16-"
"bit)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/simd/index.rst:577
msgid ""
"The same-width form supports matching float32 vectors. Widening float16 "
"inputs to float32 requires separate even/odd results and is not represented "
"by this API."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/simd/index.rst:586
msgid ""
"Computes dst = abs(src0 - src1) in a single instruction. Supported types: "
"float32, float16."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/simd/index.rst:594
msgid "Source vector register holding the input element values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/simd/index.rst:596
msgid ""
"Destination element type, e.g. \"float32\", \"float16\", \"bfloat16\", "
"\"float8_e4m3\", \"float8_e5m2\", \"float4_e2m1fn\", \"int32\", \"int16\", "
"\"uint16\", \"int8\", \"uint8\", \"int64\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/simd/index.rst:599
msgid ""
"Predicate mask; only lanes where mask[i] is true participate and are "
"written. Defaults to an all-lanes mask matching the narrower (low-lane) "
"element: the source width when widening, the target width when narrowing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/simd/index.rst:603
msgid ""
"IEEE-754 rounding mode. Valid values: - ``\"ROUND_R\"`` (default): Round to "
"nearest, ties to even (banker's rounding). - ``\"ROUND_A\"``: Round away "
"from zero. - ``\"ROUND_F\"``: Round toward -inf (floor). - ``\"ROUND_C\"``: "
"Round toward +inf (ceiling). - ``\"ROUND_Z\"``: Round toward zero "
"(truncation). - ``\"ROUND_O\"``: Round to odd (only for f32->f16). - "
"``\"ROUND_H\"``: Round half away from zero (only for hif8 conversions). Not "
"all modes are valid for every conversion pair; unused modes are ignored when "
"absent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/simd/index.rst:613
msgid ""
"saturation mode for narrow/overflow-prone conversions. - ``True`` (default): "
"Saturate to target range on overflow. - ``False``: No sat; out-of-range "
"values wrap. Appears in: all float->fp8, f32->f16/bf16, all float->int, "
"integer narrowing. Absent from: widening conversions, f16->bf16, s16->f16, "
"s32->f32 (no overflow possible)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/simd/index.rst:619
msgid ""
"Sub-register half/quarter selector for widening/narrowing conversions. For "
"even/odd 2-way splits: ``\"PART_EVEN\"`` (0), ``\"PART_ODD\"`` (1). For fp8/"
"fp4/int4 4-way splits: ``\"PART_P0\"`` (0), ``\"PART_P1\"`` (1), "
"``\"PART_P2\"`` (2), ``\"PART_P3\"`` (3). Not needed for same-width "
"conversions (e.g. f16<->bf16, s32->f32, f32->s32, f16->s16)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/simd/index.rst:624
msgid ""
"Write mode for masked-off lanes. - ``\"MODE_ZEROING\"`` (default): Inactive "
"lanes are set to zero. - ``\"MODE_MERGING\"``: Inactive lanes preserve their "
"prior value (only on mask-less int->int paths; 920R1 only for mask paths)."
msgstr ""

